---
import PineLayout from "../layouts/PineLayout.astro";
import PageHero from "../components/page/PageHero.astro";
import SectionIntro from "../components/page/SectionIntro.astro";
import Cards from "../components/page/Cards.astro";
import Prose from "../components/page/Prose.astro";
import PageCta from "../components/page/PageCta.astro";
import Schema from "../components/page/Schema.astro";
import { breadcrumb, organizationGraph } from "../lib/schema";

// Prerendered: no per-request data on this page. EmDash pins the site to
// output:"server" — its injected /_emdash/* dynamic routes would each need
// getStaticPaths() under output:"static" — so prerendering is opted into
// per page. Only /api/contact and the A/B dispatcher stay on-demand.
export const prerender = true;

// The entity page. `organizationGraph` is the canonical Organization node —
// founders, credentials and sameAs live in src/lib/schema.ts so every mention
// of "Vitops" resolves to the same entity. See content-plan/geo.md.
//
// Mission/vision/values page, not a founder spotlight. Founders get one
// short, un-interleaved bio each near the bottom — enough to back the
// Person nodes above, not the subject of the page. Don't re-promote them.
//
// Bios are written without pronouns: neither founder's are on record.
// Prior companies are deliberately unnamed — the experience is the point.
//
// Styling is framework classes only, no scoped CSS (`npx vitops docs classes`):
//   · `centered` children WITHOUT `spotlight` sit in the reading `measure`
//     track, so prose needs no max-width of its own.
//   · `rhythm` supplies vertical flow between elements — no per-element margins.
//   · `text-neutral-muted` / `-x-muted` are the functional colour tokens and
//     remap themselves in dark mode; `var(--color-mist)` does not.
//   · `split` gives equal flex columns; `flex-col @md:flex-row` stacks them.

const values = [
	{
		heading: "We publish our prices.",
		body: "Per seat, on the pricing page. Not “contact us for a quote”, which usually means the number depends on what you look like you can pay.",
	},
	{
		heading: "Month to month, 30 days' notice.",
		body: "No annual lock-in on either service. We'd rather earn it monthly than hold it contractually.",
	},
	{
		heading: "You own what we build.",
		body: "Websites on open standards, systems in your tenants, records in accounts with your name on them. If you leave, you leave with everything.",
	},
	{
		heading: "We'll tell you not to buy things.",
		body: "The first pass on a new account usually finds duplicate tools and licences nobody has opened in months. Saying so is a better first month than selling you something else.",
	},
];
---

<PineLayout
	title="About Vitops — our mission, values and how we work"
	description="Vitops is an Ottawa operations partner running the software a business operates on and the digital presence it's seen through. Our mission, what we've decided in advance, and who this suits."
>
	<Schema data={organizationGraph} />
	<Schema data={breadcrumb(["About", "/about"])} />

	<PageHero
		eyebrow="About"
		title="One partner for all of it."
		lead="Vitops runs the software a business operates on — including the accounts, licences, HR systems and vendor relationships most owners would rather not think about — and the digital presence it's seen through, under one partner rather than two vendors. What we're for, what we're aiming at, and what we've decided in advance."
		secondaryLabel="See pricing"
		secondaryHref="/pricing"
	/>

	<Prose lead>
		<p>
			Vitops is an Ottawa-based operations partner for Ontario small businesses.
			We run both halves of the work a growing company needs handled — the
			software it operates on, including the accounts, HR systems and vendor
			relationships most owners would rather not think about, and the digital
			presence it is seen through — under one partner rather than two vendors.
			The company was founded by Justin Lang and Alex Gagnon, who had each
			spent years running one of those halves for the same kind of business.
		</p>
	</Prose>

	<section class="section centered">
		<div class="spotlight">
			<SectionIntro
				eyebrow="Mission"
				title="Run the work a small business can't justify hiring for."
			/>
			<p class="font-body text-neutral-muted">
				Every growing business needs its software stack handled well, and the
				presence built on top of it. Almost none of them can justify a hire for
				either. Vitops exists to run both under one partner, at a published
				price, for businesses past the point where the admin is a real cost and
				short of the point where a dedicated hire pays for itself.
			</p>
		</div>

		<div class="rhythm mt-12 pt-8 border-t border-neutral">
			<p class="font-body text-neutral-muted">
				Working the same market from opposite ends, we kept hitting the same
				wall from different sides. One of us would fix an onboarding process and
				then wait days on whoever handled IT to create the accounts. The other
				would build a site that generated leads for a business with no process
				to answer them. Neither problem sat inside either discipline — both sat
				in the seam between them, which is exactly where nobody was accountable.
			</p>
			<p class="font-body text-neutral-muted">
				So one of us owns the software stack and the presence built on it, and
				the other owns operations — the accounts, the systems and the vendor
				relationships behind them. Each half has one person who makes the
				decisions, does the work, and picks up when something breaks, so
				neither half ever becomes somebody else's vendor.
			</p>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="section centered">
		<div class="spotlight">
			<SectionIntro
				eyebrow="Vision"
				title="One contact for whole of business operations instead of many."
			/>
			<p class="font-body text-neutral-muted">
				The gap in efficiency is trying to juggle multiple vendors and extract meaningful insights from them.
				We want the ordinary state of an Ontario small business to be that each team member can focus on what they do best instead of wasting time and money on administrative tasks, freeing up time and money for the organization to work at it's best.
			</p>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="section centered">
		<div class="spotlight">
			<SectionIntro
				eyebrow="Values"
				title="Key aspects that set us apart."
			/>
			<Cards cards={values} />
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="section centered">
		<div class="spotlight">
			<SectionIntro eyebrow="Leadership" title="Who runs it." />

			<div class="split flex-col @md:flex-row gap-10">
				<article class="rhythm">
					<h3 class="font-heading">Alex Gagnon — Co-CEO, IT</h3>
					<p class="font-body text-neutral-muted">
						A Master of Computer Science focused on artificial intelligence,
						and years building websites, search presence and the systems
						underneath them for small businesses. Microsoft Certified: Azure
						Solutions Architect Expert, and certified in Security, Compliance
						and Identity. Owns the software stack and the digital presence at
						Vitops.
					</p>
				</article>

				<article class="rhythm">
					<h3 class="font-heading">Justin Lang — Co-CEO, Operations</h3>
					<p class="font-body text-neutral-muted">
						A PhD in Population Health and more than a decade spent on how
						absence, disability and injury move through a business, then
						running HR, payroll and benefits operations for small employers.
						Owns operations at Vitops: the HR, payroll and bookkeeping systems,
						the employee lifecycle and the vendor relationships behind them.
					</p>
				</article>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="section centered">
		<div class="spotlight">
			<SectionIntro eyebrow="Fit" title="Who this works for, and who it doesn't." />
			<div class="split flex-col @md:flex-row gap-8">
				<article class="rhythm">
					<h3 class="font-heading">Works well for</h3>
					<p class="font-body text-neutral-muted">
						Small and Medium Businesses (SMBs) up to 150 people. At that size
						the software, licence and account admin has become a real cost but
						a dedicated hire still can't be justified. <a class="link" href="/industries"
							>Trades, brokerages, professional firms and clinics</a
						> are where we see that most.
					</p>
				</article>
				<article class="rhythm">
					<h3 class="font-heading">Not a good fit</h3>
					<p class="font-body text-neutral-muted">
						Small businesses under about five people who want to manage things themselves.
						Enterprise brand campaigns, where specialists are required. 
						Companies also looking to include hardware provisioning and repair.
					</p>
				</article>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="section centered">
		<SectionIntro eyebrow="Scope" title="The boundaries." />
		<p class="font-body text-neutral-muted">
			We administer systems and operations. We're not your accountant, lawyer,
			benefits broker or clinician — tax positions, legal opinions, plan design
			and clinical decisions stay with the people qualified to make them. We
			administer the systems your books, payroll and HR records live in: we
			don't do the bookkeeping, don't run the payroll, and don't make plan
			decisions. On funding, approval and amounts are decided by OCI, not by us.
		</p>
	</section>

	<section class="section centered">
		<div class="spotlight">
			<SectionIntro eyebrow="Areas" title="Where we work." />
			<p class="font-body text-neutral-muted">
				Ontario is our primary market. Ottawa is home — where we're based and
				where we show up in person, at local networking events and with local
				clients — and we support businesses elsewhere in Canada remotely.
			</p>
			<p class="font-caption text-neutral-x-muted mt-4">
				More on Ottawa:
				<a class="link" href="/seo-services-ottawa">SEO services</a>,
				<a class="link" href="/web-design-ottawa">web design</a>,
				<a class="link" href="/digital-marketing-agency-ottawa"
					>digital marketing agency</a
				>, or <a class="link" href="/contact">contact us</a> directly.
				<!-- /managed-it-services-ottawa exists as src/pages/_managed-it-services-ottawa.astro
				     but is underscore-prefixed and not a live route — add it here once re-enabled. -->
			</p>
		</div>
	</section>

	<PageCta
		title="Tell us what you're running."
		links={[
			{ label: "Managed IT services", href: "/managed-it-services" },
			{ label: "Digital marketing", href: "/digital-marketing" },
			{ label: "Pricing", href: "/pricing" },
		]}
	/>
</PineLayout>
